---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)"
---
Search for datasets from the terminal

Usage: dataseek [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  doctor      Check the environment and report readiness
  completion  Print a shell completion script to stdout
  man         Print the man page, in roff, to stdout

Options:
  -q, --quiet
          Errors and final result only

  -v, --verbose...
          Explain what is happening on stderr

      --json
          Emit JSON to stdout instead of text

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colorize output: auto, always, or never

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Color when stdout is a terminal and NO_COLOR is unset
          - always: Always color, even through a pipe (for `| less -R`)
          - never:  Never color
          
          [default: auto]

      --no-color
          Disable ANSI colors; shorthand for --color=never (or set NO_COLOR)

      --plain
          ASCII-only output; implies --color=never

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  dataseek doctor
  dataseek completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/dataseek.fish
  dataseek man | man -l -
